From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CBOC-Vita <344212538+CBOC-Vita@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:57:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 73/73] tests, ge_replay: a settings smoke test and a script that
 walks the picture rows through the replayer

portablekit_settings_smoke_tests walks every row and every value of the settings menu with no GL and no game: the typed accessor
for each value, the restart rule, save to settings.txt and reload, LEFT/RIGHT wrapping around the list, a developer override (the
row greys and keeps the override's value), the "not available" and "needs a restart" reasons, the real Menu button navigation across
the pages and rows with CIRCLE saving, and the menu drawn on a software canvas at two sizes with every value and every help line
(18 rows, 46 values).

tools/ge_replay/settings_matrix.sh replays the same GE dumps once per value of a picture row (texture filter, mipmaps, anti-aliasing
including Auto and gl_aa_auto=0, pixel lighting, effects resolution, FPS counter, resolution, frame limit, frame skip, HD textures,
movie filter, and two switches made while the replay runs) and checks each against the default picture by checksum: "differ" where
the menu promises a different picture, "same" where the row changes nothing in a replay. It needs a GE dump folder; dumps and the
pictures made from them are game data and stay out of git.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
